WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.055 --> 00:00:06.546
When Pollyanna arrived, Miss Polly was reading in her sitting room.

2
00:00:06.547 --> 00:00:11.335
She didn't bother to stand up but extended a hand for Pollyanna to shake.

3
00:00:11.336 --> 00:00:13.652
"How do you do, Pollyanna? I—"

4
00:00:13.653 --> 00:00:19.580
Pollyanna raced across the room and threw her arms around her startled relative.

5
00:00:19.581 --> 00:00:25.973
"Aunt Polly! I'm so glad you're letting me live with you!"

6
00:00:25.974 --> 00:00:31.514
Pollyanna sobbed with relief, burying her face in Aunt Polly's lap.

7
00:00:31.515 --> 00:00:38.068
"I'm sure that's true." Aunt Polly tried to loosen Pollyanna's grip around her waist.

8
00:00:38.069 --> 00:00:41.556
"Please be good enough to stand up straight.

9
00:00:41.557 --> 00:00:43.765
I don't even know what you look like."

10
00:00:43.766 --> 00:00:50.046
Pollyanna stood up at once.

11
00:00:50.047 --> 00:00:53.124
"I should explain why I'm wearing red instead of black.

12
00:00:53.125 --> 00:00:55.486
I told Nancy how Father said—"

13
00:00:55.487 --> 00:00:59.680
"Never mind what he said," Aunt Polly interrupted.

14
00:00:59.681 --> 00:01:02.352
"You've brought a trunk, I assume?"

15
00:01:02.353 --> 00:01:06.135
"Yes, indeed. I don't have many things of my own.

16
00:01:06.136 --> 00:01:09.822
But the Ladies' Aiders thought I should bring Father's books and—"

17
00:01:09.823 --> 00:01:13.125
"Pollyanna!" Aunt Polly interrupted again.

18
00:01:13.126 --> 00:01:15.781
"There's something we should get straight right away.

19
00:01:15.782 --> 00:01:20.579
I don't want to hear anything about your father."

20
00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:27.257
Pollyanna looked startled. "You mean . . . nothing at all?"

21
00:01:27.258 --> 00:01:32.715
"It's time to go upstairs to your room," Aunt Polly said, changing the subject.

22
00:01:32.716 --> 00:01:37.033
Silently, Pollyanna followed her aunt from the sitting room.

23
00:01:37.034 --> 00:01:42.803
Her eyes were filled with tears, but she bravely held her chin high.

24
00:01:42.804 --> 00:01:46.183
She thought Aunt Polly was probably being kind.

25
00:01:46.184 --> 00:01:51.168
"I'm glad Aunt Polly doesn't want to talk about Father," Pollyanna thought.

26
00:01:51.169 --> 00:01:56.354
"Maybe if I don't talk about him, I won't miss him so much."

27
00:01:56.355 --> 00:02:05.076
They were in an upstairs hallway now, and Pollyanna eagerly admired the thick rugs and pictures in gold frames.

28
00:02:05.077 --> 00:02:11.475
Open doors offered glimpses into beautifully furnished bedrooms with lace curtains at the windows.

29
00:02:11.476 --> 00:02:14.977
Pollyanna couldn't wait to see which bedroom was hers.

30
00:02:14.978 --> 00:02:19.472
"Oh, Aunt Polly, you have so many pretty things.

31
00:02:19.473 --> 00:02:23.718
You must be glad you're rich!" Pollyanna exclaimed.

32
00:02:23.719 --> 00:02:31.091
"Pollyanna!" Aunt Polly scolded. "We do not talk about money in this family!"

33
00:02:31.092 --> 00:02:36.655
Aunt Polly's instinct had been to put her niece as far away from herself as possible.

34
00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:40.366
She knew children were careless, so the attic was perfect.

35
00:02:40.367 --> 00:02:43.996
It contained nothing valuable that Pollyanna could ruin.

36
00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:51.298
Now that Aunt Polly had met Pollyanna, she'd seen that this girl was very interested in money and possessions.

37
00:02:51.299 --> 00:02:55.274
Her instinct had been right!

38
00:02:55.275 --> 00:03:02.447
Aunt Polly opened a door, and they went upstairs into the dim, hot attic.

39
00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:08.587
Pollyanna couldn't imagine why Aunt Polly was taking her someplace where it was hard to breathe.

40
00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:12.738
"Here's your room," Aunt Polly said, opening a door.

41
00:03:12.739 --> 00:03:17.118
"I see Tom has brought up your trunk. Do you have the key?"

42
00:03:17.119 --> 00:03:22.739
Pollyanna nodded. Her eyes were wide with fright.

43
00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:27.210
"When I ask a question, Pollyanna, I'd like you to speak."

44
00:03:27.211 --> 00:03:29.387
"Yes, Aunt Polly."

45
00:03:29.388 --> 00:03:36.320
"Thank you, that's better." Aunt Polly glanced at the water pitcher, which Nancy had filled.

46
00:03:36.321 --> 00:03:39.011
"I believe you have everything you need.

47
00:03:39.012 --> 00:03:45.592
I'll send Nancy to help you unpack. Supper is at six o'clock."

48
00:03:45.593 --> 00:03:50.879
Aunt Polly abruptly went downstairs, leaving Pollyanna alone.

49
00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:56.176
When Nancy came up a few minutes later, she found Pollyanna sobbing.

50
00:03:56.177 --> 00:04:02.810
"Oh, you poor lamb!" Nancy dropped to the floor and hugged Pollyanna.

51
00:04:02.811 --> 00:04:05.898
"Let's hang up your dresses."

52
00:04:05.899 --> 00:04:08.623
"I don't have many."

53
00:04:08.624 --> 00:04:11.971
"Then it'll be a quick job," Nancy said.

54
00:04:11.972 --> 00:04:18.179
Pollyanna suddenly smiled. "Well, I can be glad about that!"

55
00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:21.282
Nancy didn't know how to respond.

56
00:04:21.283 --> 00:04:26.333
She quickly unpacked Pollyanna's patched underwear and out-of-style dresses.

57
00:04:26.334 --> 00:04:31.726
Nancy suspected they'd all come from the donation box.

58
00:04:31.727 --> 00:04:36.515
"This will be a nice room," Pollyanna said, looking out a window.

59
00:04:36.516 --> 00:04:43.167
"Don't you think? I'm glad there isn't a mirror because now I can't see my freckles.

60
00:04:43.168 --> 00:04:47.846
And the view from this window is better than any picture.

61
00:04:47.847 --> 00:04:51.941
I'm so glad Aunt Polly let me have this room!"

62
00:04:51.942 --> 00:05:02.111
To Pollyanna's surprise, Nancy stifled a sob and ran downstairs.

63
00:05:02.112 --> 00:05:08.570
Left alone, Pollyanna opened the window and let in the cool, fresh air along with some flies.

64
00:05:08.571 --> 00:05:14.455
She smiled mischievously as she studied the tree outside.

65
00:05:14.456 --> 00:05:19.114
"I bet I could climb down this tree!"

66
00:05:19.115 --> 00:05:25.094
An hour later the hall clock struck six, and Nancy rang the bell for supper.

67
00:05:25.095 --> 00:05:29.763
Five minutes passed, and there was no sign of Pollyanna.

68
00:05:29.764 --> 00:05:33.689
Aunt Polly stepped into the hall and listened intently.

69
00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:38.204
For a moment she waited, tapping her foot impatiently.

70
00:05:38.205 --> 00:05:42.953
Then she swept into the dining room.

